---
name: recent_actions
description: >
  The agent's own last few actions, appended to a live decide observation
  (issue #826). Rendered by cognition.recent_actions_block() and folded into
  observe_and_decide's observation when the step loop threads a SimClock.
  Retrieval alone cannot be relied on for this: retrieve(touch=True) refreshes
  a high-importance commitment memory's recency on every hit, while the
  agent's own importance-2.0 outcome records decay out of contention -- over a
  57-minute walk, to nothing -- so an agent could read only its intentions and
  re-form them at every arrival, believing an errand it never performed was
  done. This block is a guarantee rather than a bid: it bypasses scoring
  entirely. Appended AFTER the retrieve, so it can never shift which memories
  surface (frames embed that list). The deterministic mock reads only the
  observation's first line, so this can never change a mock decision.
  Which records, and how long ago, are computed in Python (they are data);
  only the wording lives here.
inputs:
  actions:
    type: array
    description: >
      The actions to show, newest first, each {minutes, text}. `minutes` is how
      long ago it happened; 0 renders as "just now". `text` is the memory
      record verbatim -- these are the agent's own words, not prose to rewrite,
      so perform's present tense ("I am ...") is left as reflection.prompty
      wrote it.
sample:
  actions:
    - minutes: 57
      text: I traveled to Van Pelt — Moelis Reading Room.
    - minutes: 0
      text: I studied genetics for 30 minutes.
---
Recently, you:
{%- for a in actions %}
 - {% if a.minutes %}{{ a.minutes }} min ago{% else %}just now{% endif %}: {{ a.text }}
{%- endfor -%}
